  "_": [
    "Physical specifications from rl/01992, Paillard's own brochure",
    "'Lenses for 16mm Motion Picture and Television Cameras'.",
    "",
    "Its two specification tables cover the Kern-Paillard and SOM Berthiot",
    "lines, and give per lens: the catalogue number, what the lens is",
    "designed for, angle of view, minimum focusing distance, the area",
    "covered at that distance and at 20 feet, minimum diaphragm, the kind",
    "of depth-of-field scale, length at infinity, front and maximum",
    "diameter, weight and filter adapter number.",
    "",
    "Read off the rendered page. The scan's OCR interleaves the columns",
    "completely and cannot be used: it pairs each figure with the wrong",
    "lens. Every value here was read by eye from the table.",
    "",
    "The catalogue numbers come in pairs where a lens was sold in two",
    "mounts. '34 & 5' means number 34 for C mount and Vidicon cameras and",
    "number 5 for the Bolex Reflex. The Pan Cinors pair a 'C' and Vidicon",
    "number with an 'S' (Kodak) one instead.",
    "",
    "One figure is deliberately absent. The Vario-Switar 86's area covered",
    "at 20 feet at its shortest focal length reads as '17\" x 84\"' on the",
    "page, where every comparable lens is around 120 inches wide. The",
    "leading digit has not survived the scan, so the field is left out",
    "rather than published wrong.",
    "",
    "Read by scripts/extract-lens-items.mjs and shown on the lens page."
  ],
